there are so many new beauty releases  happening all the time so we gathered  some of the most hyped products from  november to test for ourselves let's  start with the brand everyone is talking  about ariana grande's rem beauty i don't  have every product but i have a decent  batch now i love miss ponytail and i  will buy anything she tells me to but we  definitely have some products here that  are underwhelming the skips for me are  the volumizing mascara and the eyeliner  the mascara was pretty clumpy and i've  tried better mascara formulas at the  drugstore the eyeliner also wasn't great  which is shocking because i feel like  that's her thing it was just skipping on  the eye and it wasn't as intensely black  as i wanted it to be everything else i  tried i loved the lip products are very  pigmented and comfortable on the lips  the plumping gloss has this really nice  minty scent and the lipstick smells like  vanilla cake i love it also i know  everyone hated the packaging but come on  this lipstick is so cute it looks like a  little astronaut the liquid shadow was  super easy to blend and looked pretty on  the eyes i will say i wish it was more  sparkly it looked a little dull for me  if you can only get one product from  this brand though get the highlighter  topper it's more on the metallic side  but not glittery at all and it looks  amazing on the skin  i freaked out when i saw that elf came  out with basically their own version of  the abh brow freeze i still love that  fluffy laminated brow look so of course  i had to get it and compare the two  mine did come super cloudy and white  looking on the website the product looks  totally clear just like the abh brow  freeze so i don't know what that's about  anyway i applied the elf brow lift on my  right brow using the specific brow lift  applicator they released with it  and already i could tell that this is  the same as the brow freeze or at least  as close as you can get it didn't take a  lot of product to get the brow looking  full and fluffy and i also love the  applicator because it came with this  little flat piece at the end to really  press the brow hairs into place i used  the abh brow freeze on my left brow so  you can see how similar the effect is i  highly highly highly recommend this if  you're into this kind of brow look  i was so confused when i saw this petri  dish looking highlighter all over tik  tok this is the huda beauty rose quartz  face gloss highlighting do and it's  essentially a cream highlighter face  gloss hybrid i've never been interested  in these kinds of products because they  tend to remove foundation and that's  pretty much what happened with this the  formula is almost tacky it's very sticky  so everywhere i applied it it was  lifting off more and more foundation the  glow it gives is actually pretty nice  but it's not worth the trouble for me  i'd rather just use a powder highlighter  purple blush has been everywhere lately  and i've been wanting to try it so bad  this is one of the purple blushes i kept  seeing the made by mitchell blursh i'm  not saying that weird that's what it's  called i was playing with fire applying  a liquid blush over my already powdered  base a purple blush nonetheless but i  did it anyway and this formula actually  blew my mind it didn't remove any  foundation it didn't get patchy and it  was so effortless to blend out i don't  know if i'm super sold on purple blush  on my skin tone i just don't think that  it's more flattering than my normal like  peachy orange blushes but it's still  pretty i definitely want more blushes  from this brand i was so intrigued by  this concealer because it's described as  a concealer serum which i've never tried  before when i was applying it with my  brush i was getting excited because it  seemed like the coverage was great it  was super creamy but then i started  blending on the rest of my face it  blended out just fine and i thought it  looked good but something weird was  happening on my under eyes specifically  on my right side the product started to  pill up and get kind of weird but it  didn't do that on my left side so i'm  confused i think it all looked better  after i set it with powder finished my  makeup and applied my setting spray but  i'm not a huge fan of this concealer yet  maybe i just have to try it again with a  different foundation i am so not a  glitter person but i saw some videos of  this particular glitter in action and  fell in love this is the la girl glitter  holic glitter topper in hollow glam oh  my god say that five times fast it has  this color shifting magic in it that  makes it look like you have nothing on  your eyes but then you move your head  and it's like purple and then blue i  don't even know how to describe it but  i'm really obsessed it has a built-in  base so you don't need to use any  glitter adhesive just apply it with your  fingers i think i would still use this  with a glitter base just for some extra  security but i'm paranoid i love this  and it's only six bucks  [Music]  [Music]
 

